 `GET /api/analyze/{sighting_id}` returns the combined sighting + tiger +
 embedding record produced by a previous analyze call.
 
+## Batch ingestion (`/api/batch`)
+
+Processes a whole raw camera-trap folder at once, reusing `/api/analyze`'s
+pipeline per file -- no logic is duplicated.
+
+- **Default folder**: `D:\penchimages` (override with the
+  `PUGA_RAW_IMAGES_DIR` env var, or pass `"folder"` in the request body).
+- `POST /api/batch/analyze` `{folder?, camera_id?, recursive?, limit?}` --
+  scans the folder, dedupes by file content hash (so a copied/renamed
+  duplicate from a mixed-up SD card is recognized), and for each new file:
+  - **no animal detected** -> the *original* file is moved (never deleted)
+    to `data/quarantine/{batch_id}/`, status `quarantined`.
+  - **animal detected** -> routed through the same AUTO_MATCH / REVIEW /
+    POSSIBLE_NEW decision as a single `/api/analyze` call; `processed` if
+    a sighting was created, `needs_review` otherwise. Original file is
+    left in place.
+  - Any per-file error (bad image, AI deps missing, etc.) is caught and
+    recorded as `failed` on that file only -- one bad file never aborts
+    the whole batch.
+  - Already-seen files (matched by hash, from any earlier batch) are
+    skipped and marked `duplicate`, so re-running against the same folder
+    is safe/idempotent.
+- `GET /api/batch` -- list all batch_ids run so far.
+- `GET /api/batch/{batch_id}` -- summary + per-file results for one run.
+- `GET /api/batch/config` -- shows the currently configured raw-images folder.
+- `GET /api/batch/quarantine` -- list all quarantined (blank) images.
+- `POST /api/batch/quarantine/{id}/restore` -- move a quarantined file back
+  to its original location (409 if something already exists there).
+
